      A Although as indicated in Unit 14 Chinese verbs do not express
      tense they are often linked with an aspect marker which may indicate
      the completion, experience, continuation, etc. of an action. With the
      exception of    zài (see below) aspect markers are placed directly after
      the verb.

      The most common aspect markers are:

               le       completed action
               guo      past experience
               zài      an action in progress
