                            noun or a spatial/temporal relationship to the noun
                            (e.g. ‘on’, ‘in’, ‘outside’, ‘above’, etc.). A noun followed
                            by a postposition is called a postpostional phrase, which
                            usually indicates location or time, and resembles a
                            prepositional phrase in English (e.g. the preposi-
                            tional phrase ‘on the table’ in English is rendered in
